 Wow. This is going very well. My wizard, Gray Alys, had a good start --
her second spellbook was magic missile, and there were two general stores
and an altar by the fourth floor. She converted the altar and cleaned out
the stores, netting a silver dagger that would later turn out to be +1,
and a spellbook of sleep. Now having my favorite spell in her arsenal, she
dumped the elven mithril that she found lying about early on, so as to
focus on spellcasting.

 She entered the first floor of the mines at experience level 3, with her
large cat Therial and her new pet horse, and intrinsic speed from a wand
on all three. The gnomes and dwarves didn't stand a chance. A little more
loot and slightly better armor, and she went back up and then down to the
fifth floor of the Mazes of Menace, where she encountered a bones file.
This was left originally by my valkyrie Jirel -- whom you may recall had a
sacfest accident involving a blindfold that wasn't on, a floating eye, a
fire-engraved E-word, and a damn green elf at the back of the crowd that
didn't respect it. This was also a bones pile for my orcish rogue,
Grindleguts, who had found it, killed half of the summoned monsters, snuck
into Jirel's stash room and locked himself in to outfit himself while his
pets wiped out the remainder of the monsters, then stepped out and was
killed by a resurrected troll and an invisible dwarf, handing them a wand
of fire in the process. Grindley didn't add much loot himself, so it's
really more like a single bones pile.. But a huge one from a
"clean-dungeon" type player.. (I hate to leave even armor and weapons
around, since it just makes average monsters tougher)

 Gray Alys fled back up and made some holy water and blessed the four id
scrolls she had got from the shops and used one to id the three amulets
from the second floor shop in hopes of reflection.. The first scroll id'ed
everything, woohoo! Amulets were one vs. poison, one restful sleep, and
hey! One life saving. Putting that and and a ring of stealth on, she went
down again and sleep-spelled first the troll and then the invisible dwarf,
who never got to use his wand of fire, thankfully.
 She spent quite some time moving her stash down and BUC id'ing all of
that gigantic pile from Jirel, and now she's got black dragon scale mail,
elven boots, a crapload of wands and spells, and now she is the first
wizard I've played in I don't know how long who just got Magicbane from a
helpful dwarf who wandered in. Jirel's luckstone got vaporized by a #loot
accident, along with a couple of other things, but I can scarcely complain
considering what I've got already. It's too bad I've no use for a +4
Excalibur, Mjollnir, or Demonbane. No wishing for artifacts later, I
suppose. :)
 I still have to get reflection and foo-proof her cloak of MR at least,
but with a +3 small shield and the rest of her -4 AC she still has 0%
failure on force bolt, MM, and sleep, and thanks to a blessed gain
energy's extra 15 or so, she has 86 SP to fire them off with. Woohoo! Time
to do Soko-ban, and then head to Mine's end for a luckstone.

 Now I know something nasty is bound to happen, I'm sure of it. Any bets
on what kills her?

